# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Manufacturer documents are copyrighted and are never committed.
# See docs/CORPUS_LICENSING.md. The manifest under corpus/manifest/ describes
# these files; the bytes themselves stay on the machine that acquired them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
corpus/documents/*
corpus/_staging/
corpus/snapshots/

# The directory itself is tracked, via its README only, so a fresh clone shows
# where documents go instead of leaving the user to guess.
!corpus/documents/README.md

# Belt and braces: no document artefact should ever enter history, wherever
# it happens to be sitting. The pre-commit hook in .githooks/ enforces this
# too, because a .gitignore alone does not stop `git add -f`.
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.doc
*.docx

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local infrastructure and secrets — never commit.
# Policy and placeholders live in docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md and *.example files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.local.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
